.TH MORPH 1 "2026-10-30" "morph 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
morph \- privacy-focused offline file format converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B morph
[\fB--in\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--to\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB--out\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B morph doctor
.B morph completion \fIshell\fR
.B morph version
.SH DESCRIPTION
morph is an offline-only CLI tool for converting between many file formats.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --in " " \fIFILE\fR
Input file, use - for stdin, glob pattern, or directory
.TP
.BR --to " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Target format
.TP
.BR --out " " \fIFILE\fR
Output file, use - for stdout
.TP
.BR --list
List supported conversions
.TP
.BR --list-json
List supported conversions as JSON
.TP
.BR --force
Overwrite existing output
.TP
.BR --quiet
Minimal output
.TP
.BR --verbose
Verbose output
.TP
.BR --recursive
Process directories recursively
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
morph --in image.png --to jpg
Convert image
.TP
morph --in "*.txt" --to pdf
Batch convert
.TP
cat data.json | morph --in - --to yaml --out -
Pipe conversion
.SH AUTHOR
AliFnieer
